dwave" content-desc='One hot summer day a fox was walking through an orchard. He saw a bunch of ripe grapes hanging from a high vine. The grapes looked sweet and juicy.&#10;&#10;"I want those grapes," said the fox. He jumped up, but he could not reach them. He jumped again and again, but the grapes were too high.&#10;&#10;At last the fox stopped jumping. He looked at the grapes and said, "Those grapes are sour anyway. I do not want them."&#10;&#10;Then he walked away.&#10;&#10;Sometimes people say that something is not good when they cannot have it. We call this "sour grapes." It means that we make excuses when we fail.&#10;&#10;The story teaches us an important lesson: it is better to try your best and accept the result honestly than to pretend you did not want it.' checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[42,590][1038,2207]" /></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></hierarchy>
